# Frontend Guidelines

- Always prefer functional React components (no class components).  
- Use Bootstrap markup and CSS. Don't add unnecessary classes. 
- Use Twitter Bootstrap classes in most if not all cases and then if nothing works use tailwind CSS.
- Avoid inline styles; use CSS modules if custom styles are necessary.  
- Components should have clear, descriptive naming.
- Use React Bootstrap for navigation and make the navigation driven by JSON hard-coded in the nav
- Use React Bootstrap library for making components, refer to their documentation on what components are available.
- For all icons use bootstrap-icons
- do not use react-bootstrap-icons use bootstrap-icons instead for all icons